---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from "../lib/constants";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The rules for using Marked, including subscriptions, cancellation and what Marked is and isn't."
>
  <p>
    These terms apply when you use Marked, a trade journal for forex and crypto
    traders. By creating an account or using the service, you agree to them.
  </p>

  <h2>What Marked is, and isn't</h2>
  <p>
    Marked helps you record trades and understand your own results. It is a
    journaling and analytics tool. It is <strong>not</strong> financial,
    investment or tax advice, and it doesn't tell you what to trade. Trading
    forex and crypto carries a real risk of loss, and decisions you make are
    yours. The figures Marked shows depend on what you enter, and live exchange
    rates come from a third party, so check anything important yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    Keep your sign-in details safe and give us accurate information. You're
    responsible for what happens under your account. You must be at least 18.
  </p>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    Your journal belongs to you. You give us permission to store and process it
    only so we can provide Marked to you. How we handle it is described in the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Plans and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      There is a Free plan and a paid Pro plan. What each includes is shown on
      the <a href="/#pricing">pricing section</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Pro is billed in advance, in Nigerian naira, through Paystack, monthly or
      yearly depending on the plan you choose.
    </li>
    <li>
      Pro renews automatically at the end of each period until you cancel. We
      charge the card you provided.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can cancel at any time from the Billing page. You keep Pro until the
      end of the period you've paid for and you won't be charged again.
    </li>
    <li>
      If we change a price, we'll tell you before it applies to you, and you can
      cancel before it does.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a payment fails, Pro is paused until it succeeds or you subscribe
      again. Your data stays in your account.
    </li>
    <li>Refunds are covered in the <a href="/refunds">refund policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Using Marked fairly</h2>
  <p>
    Don't misuse the service: no breaking the law, probing for security holes,
    overloading it, trying to reach other people's data, or reselling access.
    We may suspend an account that does.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep Marked running and your data safe, but we can't promise it
    will never be interrupted or free of errors. Keep your own copy of anything
    you can't afford to lose.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits on our responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, Marked is provided "as is", and we aren't
    liable for trading losses or for indirect or consequential losses. Where we
    are liable, it is limited to what you paid us in the 12 months before the
    problem. Nothing here limits rights you have by law that can't be limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account whenever you like from your profile. We may end
    or suspend an account that breaks these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. If a change matters, we'll tell you in the app or
    by email before it takes effect. Carrying on after that means you accept it.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria.</p>

  {
    SUPPORT_EMAIL ? (
      <>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : null
  }
</LegalLayout>